Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 17:22:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] Run the sky view factor processes with joblib (no main
 guard needed)

The svf azimuths ran in a spawn multiprocessing pool, which re-imports the
main script: a script without an `if __name__ == "__main__":` guard (all
TopoPyScale_examples scripts) hung as soon as CPU_cores > 1. joblib's
loky workers (joblib comes with scikit-learn) do not re-import the main
script and memory-map the large arrays. Threads are no alternative: the
sweep holds the GIL and runs slower with 2 threads than serially.

Same results; test running an unguarded script in a subprocess.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012FMkEYDUJxvxmd3SbUsJfP
